[al:新概念英语第二册]
[ti:89. A Slip of the Tongue]
[00:00.480]Passage 89 | 文章八十九
[00:02.370]A slip of the tongue. | 口误。
[00:05.075]People will do anything to see a free show, | 人们会不惜一切来看一场免费演出，
[00:09.785]even if it is a bad one. | 即使那是一场糟糕的演出。
[00:12.240]When the news got around that a variety show would be presented at our local cinema | 当消息传开，说我们当地的电影院将上演一场综艺节目，
[00:18.260]by the P and U Bird Seed Company, | 由 P 和 U 鸟食公司主办时，
[00:21.225]we all rushed to see it. | 我们都争相去观看。
[00:23.840]We had to queue for hours to get in, | 我们排了好几个小时的队才得以入场，
[00:27.190]and there must have been several hundred people present | 而且在演出开始前，
[00:30.640]just before the show began. | 肯定有几百人到场。
[00:33.245]Unfortunately, | 不幸的是，
[00:35.435]the show was one of the dullest we have ever seen. | 那场演出是我们看过的最乏味的演出之一。
[00:39.495]Those who failed to get in need not have felt disappointed, | 那些未能入场的人大可不必感到失望，
[00:43.865]as many of the artists who should have appeared | 因为许多本该出场的艺术家
[00:46.730]did not come. | 并未到场。
[00:48.275]The only funny things we heard that evening | 那晚我们听到的唯一有趣的事情
[00:51.810]came from the advertiser at the beginning of the program. | 来自节目开始时的广告商。
[00:55.385]He was obviously very nervous, | 他显然非常紧张，
[00:58.490]and for some minutes | 几分钟里，
[00:59.925]stood awkwardly before the microphone. | 他笨拙地站在麦克风前。
[01:03.025]As soon as he opened his mouth, | 他刚一开口，
[01:05.635]everyone burst out laughing. | 大家都哄堂大笑起来。
[01:08.220]We all know what the poor man should have said, | 我们都知道那个可怜人本该说什么，
[01:12.010]but what he actually said was, | 但他实际说的是：
[01:15.205]“This is the poo and E seed bird company. | “这是便便和E种子鸟公司。
[01:19.110]Good ladies, evening and gentlemen.” | 女士们，先生们，晚上好。”